<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28456" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlas</span></b> , ănis and
		ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέλας</span>
		(black). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The name of several rivers.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A river of Bœotia</i>, now <i>Mavropotami</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 2,
				103, 106, § 230</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Q. N. 3, 25, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 7,
			273</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A river of Thrace</i>, now <i>Kavatch</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 40, 5</span></i>; Mela, 2, 2, 8;
				<i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				2, 274</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11, 18, §
			43</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>A river of Sicily</i>, now <i>Nocito</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacrorumque Melan pascua laeta boum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 476</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>A river of Cappadocia</i>, now <i>Jochmah Su</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 4, 4, §
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>A river of Cilicia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 27,
				22, § 93</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A son of Phryxus</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>One of the Etruscan seamen whom Bacchus changed into
				dolphins</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 134</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
